severity: low
evidence: sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:158-166 — signature reads `alpha=None`, while the docstring at sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:183-184 says `alpha : float, default=1.0`. sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:241 then does `distance_matrix /= alpha`, which would raise `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for /=: 'ndarray' and 'NoneType'` if the default were ever used. Only the internal call sites currently pass `self.alpha`, so it does not blow up in practice, but the signature is misleading.
